WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.754
An S M executes the threads in a block in
groups called warps.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:09.590
In the eight rows by thirty-two columns
case, the block has one warp.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.429
Each lane identifies one thread in that
warp.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.001
A word offset counts four byte values from
the start of the array.

00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:20.350
The first eight lanes read consecutive
columns.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.700
Their eight values fit in one thirty-two
byte sector.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.015
The transpose swaps row and column.

00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:30.795
In the output, these lanes write eight
words apart.

00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:34.434
The same eight lanes now touch eight
distinct sectors.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.383
The warp address model shows four sectors
for reads and thirty-two for writes across

00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:41.137
all lanes.

00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:43.210
The model groups addresses.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.842
Measuring traffic on a GPU also requires
accounting for caches and the instructions

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:50.100
the hardware runs.
